/Title (The Moving Average Convergence Divergence \(MACD\) works by finding the difference between short-term and long-term exponential moving averages, which helps identify changes in momentum and possible trend reversals when the lines cross each other. Additionally, volatility works by measuring how much the stock price deviates from its average using statistical methods like standard deviation, indicating the level of risk, where higher volatility means greater price fluctuations and higher risk, while lower volatility indicates more stable price movement. Together, these indicators transform complex historical data into simple trends and signals, helping users make informed investment decisions.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 2270 0 R
/Next 2375 0 R
>>
